timestamp=2026-11-04T09:55:04.510Z level=INFO run=714ca7dd message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Also look at PM10 side - is there any other station that fits clue 1/2/3 better in a different way?\n# For example, ST040 has resid-wind correlation very strong (-0.673) which is even stronger than ST039. Also means deviations align neatly with wind. That’s clue 3-like. But ST040 also has muted swings and lag issues - multiple problems. Which one is the cleaner \"third\"?\n# The third clue says specifically: \"appears ordinary in aggregate, but its remaining deviations line up a bit too neatly with one environmental driver\"\n# ST039: corr0 is good (0.758), cv_ratio not muted (1.759, actually more variable than peers) - so \"ordinary in aggregate\" in terms of tracking peers well. That fits. ST040: corr0 is poor (0.385), so not \"ordinary in aggregate\" - it’s already odd in aggregate. That doesn’t fit clue 3 as written. So ST039 is better for clue 3.\n# ST040’s muted swings (cv_ratio 0.774) could fit clue 2 - but corr0 is only 0.385, so not very \"plausible point-by-point\". ST051 has much better corr0 for clue 2.\n# ST040’s lag shift gives best_corr 0.606 at lag+1 - improvement exists. But compared to ST058, ST058’s corr0 is much lower (0.279) with clear lag structure. ST058 is the cleaner \"rhythm\" case.\n# So the set {ST058, ST051, ST039} looks coherent for the three distinct clues.\npass\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
